5e"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Each counter gains a persisted journald cursor and its scan reads only entries after it ... adding the new matches to the persisted total.'","'(cold-start seeding, lost-history suppression) are preserved' — cold-start is preserved, but the old-format-total-without-cursor case on first post-deploy run is not explicitly named.","T4(a): a change to the persisted state shape where the first post-deploy run reads a total but finds no cursor."],"finding":"R1 introduces new persisted state (a per-counter journald cursor alongside the existing cumulative total) but does not describe the transition for an already-running host whose state file has a total but no cursor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdc6a7c27102ae9e7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair R1 — persisted cursor / maintained total","norm_id":"neb34d9f3ba025ea7","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["First run after deploy on the live host: state file has an old cumulative total, new code expects a cursor; if treated as cold-start the total may be re-seeded, if treated as present the delta may be wrong."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct R3's rationale to note that git fetch (autodeploy.sh:798) is already `timeout`-bounded; only git clone (:787) is unbounded — the R3 repair is the unit-file TimeoutStartSec, not the git calls themselves.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan R3: 'autodeploy.sh makes unbounded git clone / git fetch calls. Identical failure mode, one line.'","autodeploy.sh:798 `if ! timeout \"$FETCH_TIMEOUT\" git -C \"$MIRROR_DIR\" fetch -q --prune ...`","autodeploy.sh:787 `if ! git clone -q \"$MIRROR_URL\" \"$MIRROR_DIR\" ...` (no timeout)"],"finding":"R3's supporting rationale states autodeploy.sh makes 'unbounded git clone / git fetch calls', but the git fetch at autodeploy.sh:798 is already bounded by `timeout \"$FETCH_TIMEOUT\"`; only the git clone at :787 is unbounded.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb87990523a0ebc2e","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair R3","norm_id":"nb6109f0d36b996be","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or implementer treats the git fetch as an unbounded target and re-bounds an already-bounded call, or is confused about which call the 'one line' fix addresses."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword R3 to: 'autodeploy.sh's git clone (:787) is unbounded (git fetch at :798 is already timeout-wrapped); regardless, the same oneshot latch applies, fixed by one line adding TimeoutStartSec to the .service unit.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Add an acceptance criterion that asserts each R4 sibling call (IMDS curls, git ls-remote, du) carries a finite bound, verified behaviorally or by asserting the rendered/invoked bound.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["R4 lists 'The IMDS token/region/instance-id curls, the git ls-remote mirror comparison ... and the du ... all run unbounded ... Each is bounded.'","AC1-AC3 concern only journal scans; AC4/AC5 concern systemd timeouts; AC6 is regression; AC7 is documentation — none exercise the R4 sibling bounds.","E6(c): every acceptance criterion maps to a step, but here a deliverable (R4) has no covering criterion; E1(a): described deliverable with no covering criterion."],"finding":"R4 bounds several sibling unbounded calls (IMDS token/region/instance-id curls, the git ls-remote mirror comparison, and the du over data-disk entries) but no acceptance criterion verifies these bounds were applied.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc4a2677cbfae2c4a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair R4 / Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"na2cffe0c97694a90","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer bounds the journal scans and systemd timeouts but forgets one of the R4 sibling curls; nothing in the AC set catches it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add AC8: 'Each R4 sibling call (IMDS metadata curls, the git ls-remote mirror comparison, and the du over data-disk entries) carries a finite wall-clock bound, asserted by exercising the script with a hanging stub for each and confirming the probe terminates within the timer period.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Specify how R1 interprets an existing old-format offset file (cumulative total, no cursor) on the first post-upgrade run — e.g. treat a missing cursor as a seed that anchors the cursor to the journal tail and publishes 0 for that interval — and add an AC asserting the old->new format transition counts each marker exactly once across the upgrade.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["R1: 'Each counter gains a persisted journald cursor and its scan reads only entries after it ... adding the new matches to the persisted total.'","R1: 'every documented behaviour (cold-start seeding, lost-history suppression) are preserved; only the read volume changes'","observability.sh:885-894 persists a cumulative integer total (`prev=$(cat offset_file)`, `echo total > offset_file`) with no cursor field — so an existing file on the upgrade run carries a total and no cursor.","AC2 verifies steady-state interval correctness and AC6 verifies contract preservation, but neither pins the behaviour on the run that first reads an old-format file."],"finding":"R1 changes the persisted counter representation (cumulative total -> persisted journald cursor + maintained total) but does not specify how the FIRST run of the new script interprets an EXISTING old-format offset file (a total with no cursor). Such a file is neither a cold start (file present) nor lost history, yet the plan only claims cold-start seeding and lost-history suppression are 'preserved'. The old->new file-format transition is the actual migration and is unaddressed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbdec252b638fc4e5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair R1; AC2/AC6","norm_id":"nb963f9101c02b6d1","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The new script deploys to a host whose /var/lib/rebar/*-offset files were written by the old script; on the first post-upgrade run the counter must not double-count a whole retention window nor silently drop the metric."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that when a counter's persisted state lacks a cursor (old format or absent), the new code seeds the cursor to the current journal tail and publishes 0 for that run (same as cold start), so no retention window is retro-counted; add an AC covering this transition.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the cursor and cumulative total are persisted as a single atomic commit (e.g. one file written via write-to-temp-then-rename), so a mid-write SIGKILL from TimeoutStartSec leaves either the old pair or the new pair, never a mixed state.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Each counter gains a persisted journald cursor and its scan reads only entries after it ... adding the new matches to the persisted total.'","Plan: 'On timeout, read failure, or an unusable cursor, the cursor is NOT advanced and NOTHING is published for that metric.' — states cursor non-advancement but not that total+cursor are committed as one atomic unit under a mid-write kill.","R2 introduces a SIGKILL path (TimeoutStartSec) that can interrupt the persist step at any point."],"finding":"R1 introduces a new persisted per-counter journald cursor AND a persisted cumulative total that must be written together each interval, but the plan does not specify that this write is atomic. R2 adds a finite TimeoutStartSec that SIGKILLs a hung run; if that kill lands after the cursor is advanced but before the total is updated (or vice-versa), the persisted state becomes internally inconsistent and the next run's total-prev delta is silently wrong — the same 'plausible wrong number' failure R1 explicitly rejects for the timeout-alone repair.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd16985bd3b234b93","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair R1 — 'the persisted total ... adding the new matches to the persisted total' / 'the cursor is NOT advanced'","norm_id":"nedf47e0440fc0145","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A slow scan is killed by TimeoutStartSec after the cursor file is rewritten but before the total file is rewritten; the next run reads a stale total against an advanced cursor and publishes a delta that under- or over-counts, defeating AC2/AC3."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Persist the (cursor, total) pair together in one state file written atomically (temp-file + rename); on any failure/timeout neither is advanced. Add an AC asserting the delta stays correct across a run interrupted mid-persist.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the retire/reset path for the persisted cursor state: what happens on an unusable/rotated-past cursor (reseed vs stall) and how the state is cleared on re-provision.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan enumerates CREATE (cold-start seeding) and UPDATE (append) but the RETIRE leg is not addressed for the new persisted-cursor state.","'lost-history suppression' is preserved but the plan does not state whether an unusable/rotated-past cursor is cleared/reseeded or simply left."],"finding":"R1's persisted cursor/total state has no defined RETIRE/cleanup or reset path. The plan documents cold-start seeding and lost-history suppression but does not say what happens to a stale cursor if journald rotates past it, if a counter is removed, or on host re-provisioning — whether the state file is garbage-collected or how an operator resets it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f047de02e3bddc06e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair R1 — cursor state lifecycle","norm_id":"n953c5e86b31f4d72","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["journald rotates and the persisted cursor points to a purged entry; without a defined reset the counter could stall permanently (nothing published forever) rather than reseeding."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that an unusable cursor triggers a cold-start reseed (matching existing lost-history semantics) rather than a permanent stall, and note the state file lives at a fixed path replaced on re-provision by user_data.sh.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the R1 per-scan wall-clock timeout as a default value/relation (e.g. comfortably less than the finite start timeout, w